                                "sense_id": "a8c97aab-a6a0-3990-9920-3456b342582f",
                                "text": "“You bad!” and Huckleberry began to snuffle too. “Consound it, Tom Sawyer, you’re just old pie, ’longside o’ what I am. Oh, lordy, lordy, lordy, I wisht I only had half your chance.”"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b0b53190-7ef3-426d-8af6-beaca66a2a55",
                                "sense_id": "a8c97aab-a6a0-3990-9920-3456b342582f",
                                "text": "He held his eye there as much as a minute; then he raised up and sighed, and says, ‘Consound it, I don't seem to understand this thing, no way; however, I'll tackle her again.’"
                            }
